module gunbc.extdeps_subject_ref_facts_seed_growth

import gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_model { RoadmapNodeId }
import gunbc.seed_growth { SeedGrowthJustification }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }

// FORWARD-FREEZE RECEIPT for the hand Rust added by giving the substrate a TYPED read of an
// ExternalModelScope data declaration's subject (roadmap node extdeps-subject-ref-facts-host-census,
// rn_01M7NQG5SWMS74ZGXDH6X55TQ8). Authored because gunbc.seed_growth_admission seed_growth_forward_freeze_policy_note
// makes unenumerated hand growth in src/v1 a stop-line, and this change adds a hand-written census
// producer. It is a declared row, never a silent escape hatch (gunbc.design_argument::self_hosting).
//
// WHAT THE CHANGE IS, AND WHAT IT IS NOT. It is a NEW host census -- there is no existing read it
// narrows. A keyed `decl_facts_at` over an ExternalModelScope exposes only flat authored_string_lexemes:
// there is no subject/declaration/module_path field edge and record_field_projection is Absent, so a
// typed subject read cannot be built from it substrate-side. The reason is measured, not argued:
// marshal_decl_fact_node(DataItem) routes through marshal_data_initializer_projection, ctx.lookup_fn_node
// is None for extdeps scopes never loaded into the interpreter, so it falls to
// constructor_resolution_refused_projection, and marshal_plain_record_projection fails closed unless the
// type resolves in the importing module's type env. eval_extdeps_subject_ref_facts therefore reads the
// AUTHORED parse tree directly, over the same fail-closed walk the type census consults
// (decls_parse_only_fail_closed), and never through the typechecking marshal -- so it can answer where
// the marshal refuses. It returns the subject REFERENCE as typed data; it does NOT resolve it (that is
// dp-m3-subject-ref-resolved, the consumer this census is the prerequisite for).
//
// WHY IT IS RUST AND NOT .dag. The read is a host walk over a prepared inventory the substrate cannot
// name -- the same seam gunbc.decl_facts_shared_memo_seed_growth records one layer over. The refusal has
// to be decided on the side of the seam where the authored parse tree still exists as host rows: once a
// non-literal subject crosses the typechecking marshal it becomes a refusal with no shape, and the
// per-row typed `SubjectNotLiteral { why }` -- which names whether the offending node is a named
// reference or another shape, on the subject / declaration / module_path / decl_name path -- could not be
// produced substrate-side. Refusing PER ROW (each non-literal row typed, located by its declaring
// module_path/decl_name/rel_path, and countable) rather than erroring the whole census is what lets the
// consumer run on the rows that ARE readable while the indirect rows (the live corpus carries several)
// stay visible and guessed-free. The whole census still ERRORS only on an unparseable source.
//
// WHAT IS NOT COUNTED HERE. The interpreter arm (free_call.extdeps_subject_ref_facts) is a macro arm
// inside v1_interpreter's v1_builtin_arms and is not a citable declaration; it is named here rather than
// omitted, because a receipt that counts only what the roster can cite under-reports its own growth. The
// private helpers beside the eval (extdeps_subject_ref_rows, extdeps_subject_ref_row, extdeps_record_field,
// extdeps_shape_is_named_reference, extdeps_is_external_model_scope) and the host-side mirror types
// (SubjectNotLiteralWhy, ExtdepsSubjectRead, ExtdepsSubjectRefRow, ExtdepsSubjectRefPopulation) are the
// eval's own implementation, not separate census authorities, and are likewise disclosed rather than
// itemized. THE THREE GENERATED FILES IN THE DIFF ARE PROJECTIONS AND THEIR AUTHORITIES ARE IN IT TOO,
// which is what keeps them out of this roster: v1_interpreter_dispatch_generated.rs projects
// gunbc.v1.v1_interpreter_primitive_surface, v1_compiler_infer_method.rs projects
// v1.compiler.infer_method, and std_primitive_projection.rs projects std.primitive_projection. Each is
// REGENERATED by the v1 compiler (dag/gunbc/instruments/generated_artifact_gate.dag main_wet), never
// hand-edited.
data extdeps_subject_ref_facts_seed_growth_justification: SeedGrowthJustification = SeedGrowthJustification {
  hand_authored_declarations: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.coproduct_reflection", decl_name: "eval_extdeps_subject_ref_facts", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1.compiler.infer_method", decl_name: "builtin_function_registry", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "std.primitive_projection", decl_name: "primitive_extdeps_subject_ref_facts", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.std.decl_index", decl_name: "ExtdepsSubjectRefFact", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.std.decl_index", decl_name: "SubjectNotLiteralWhy", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.std.decl_index", decl_name: "extdeps_subject_ref_facts", field: WholeDeclaration }
  ],
  reason: "A typed read of the AUTHORED parse tree that the typechecking marshal refuses to produce is a property of the host that holds the parse tree. The census is the only route by which an ExternalModelScope subject reaches the substrate as typed fields: substrate-side, marshal_decl_fact_node falls to constructor_resolution_refused_projection for extdeps scopes (ctx.lookup_fn_node is None), so record_field_projection is Absent and the subject is unreadable except as a flat lexeme soup. The refusal SHAPE is the correctness content. eval_extdeps_subject_ref_facts returns a CLOSED typed sum -- SubjectLiteral carries subject_module_path/subject_decl_name; SubjectNotLiteral carries a SubjectNotLiteralWhy naming which node on the subject -> declaration -> module_path/decl_name path is missing, a named reference, or the wrong connective -- because a non-literal row must stay typed, located and countable so dp-m3-subject-ref-resolved can tell a readable subject from an indirect one and NEVER resolve a guessed position. A String `why` would let a consumer re-parse it and let a new arm compile silently; a closed sum makes each arm a declaration. Refusal is PER ROW, not whole-census, because the live corpus carries several indirect subjects and a whole-census error would make the census -- and its consumer -- unable to run at all; the whole census still errors only on an unparseable source (decls_parse_only_fail_closed).\n\nENUMERATED RATHER THAN COUNTED. The six entries are the citable census surface (the eval, its BuiltinSignature, its primitive identity, and the census type / refusal sum / fn). The interpreter arm and the eval's private helpers and host mirror types are disclosed above, not itemized; they are implementation, not separate census authorities. The three generated files are projections of authorities that are themselves in this list, so they are not hand growth.\n\nEXECUTING EVIDENCE, not a shape argument: test.claim.extdeps_subject_ref_facts_witness reads a self-contained fixture through the census and requires, over the same population, one row read as SubjectLiteral carrying the exact authored subject.declaration as typed fields AND one row refused as SubjectNotLiteral with why SubjectNamedReference, plus a positive control that the census still sees both rows so the two arm assertions cannot pass vacuously.",
  owning_dissolution_lane: "v1-hand-queue-drain" as RoadmapNodeId,
  trigger: "Delete the eval and its roster rows when an EMITTED v2 fold resolves an ExternalModelScope data declaration's subject IN-DAG -- i.e. marshal_data_initializer_projection no longer falls to constructor_resolution_refused_projection for extdeps scopes because the scope is loaded so ctx.lookup_fn_node resolves the subject type in the importing module's type env and record_field_projection is Present -- at which point a typed subject read is an ordinary modeled projection over a loaded scope and needs no host producer at all. This receipt dissolves only then: until the scope is loaded, no substrate-side read can see the subject, so deleting the eval earlier would leave dp-m3-subject-ref-resolved with no subject source.",
  current_boundary: "One pure function of its declared pool roots. eval_extdeps_subject_ref_facts walks the pool roots through decls_parse_only_fail_closed over the top-level DataItems -- the same fail-closed parse walk and the same shared-artifact accounting the type census (data_decl_type_facts) consults -- keeps the rows whose declared type head is ExternalModelScope, reads each subject.declaration module_path / decl_name off the AUTHORED parse tree (never through the typechecking marshal, which refuses for extdeps scopes), and marshals each row as a Value::Variant of the ExtdepsSubjectRefFact sum in the canonical (module_path, decl_name) order the population read already carries. It holds nothing, adds no walk beyond the census walk, and cannot answer where the walk refuses: the pool-root defect line-stop (PoolRootContributesNothing) fires first, and an unparseable source is a census-wide error rather than a silent row drop. It does NOT resolve any subject -- it returns the subject reference as typed data, literal or refused-and-located."
}
